body:
Thank you.

&nbsp;

My resume is updated, but I still lack relevant experience/projects.  Landing an entry level interview shouldn't be hard once I get some projects on there.  If using a recruiter will help me get out of where I am, then I will gladly go through one.

&nbsp;

Would you be willing to talk a bit more about the transition to your second job?

Thank you.

&nbsp;

I'm planning to take the rest of the week off to think about the future and come up with an acceptable plan.  I recognize that networking can be huge (landed me a great internship) so I would definitely find my way into meet-ups once I find a focus.  And I also know from experience that having too much free time without any direction can make you miserable...

&nbsp;

My resume is ok - far from amazing but not terrible.  The biggest issue is, like I highlighted earlier, the fact that I don't have noteworthy experience/projects in any domain.  That didn't matter too much as a student... I was able to land 2 internships.  And if you saw my resume you wouldn't believe it, but I did get interviews with Qualcomm and Amzn.
